{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": "Held-out v6 (2026-10-12). Written before any model was run on it, and frozen: no rule, prompt or threshold may be chosen by looking at its failures. Every meeting carries `context`, the utterances its decision was settled in, which the runner stores and the decision cites as `source_utterance_ids` -- so a change that reads them can be measured, while the code as it stands ignores them. 22 of 60 cases are `terse_*`: the statement B would write leaves out what it is about (\"B안으로 확정한다\", \"2주 미루기로 했다\", \"없던 걸로 한다\") and only the context says it; `terse_new` pairs such a statement with a past decision it does not continue, so reading the context must not invent a thread. The other 38 have full statements (unchanged, modified, reversed, new_same_domain, distractor, chain), to catch what reading the context would break. Labels follow dataset.py. No statement repeats one in an earlier set. Written by the engine's author after reading a real meeting where \"온보딩은 B안으로 확정한다\" did not thread; the cases built on that meeting were rewritten in other domains. Not independently labelled.",
